WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:04.480
All right, now that we've seen how we create the pickup

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.160
and add score and things like that, what we're going to do

3
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:10.279
now is we're going to use Unreal Motion Graphics so that we

4
00:00:10.279 --> 00:00:14.160
can create the interface that's going to go on our screen

5
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.440
to show the user their score and the remaining time.

6
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.559
Now, to use this, what we're going to do first

7
00:00:19.559 --> 00:00:23.000
is we are going to create a new Widget Blueprint class

8
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.879
and name it HUD UMG.

9
00:00:24.879 --> 00:00:26.600
We're going to do this by right clicking

10
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.760
in the content browser, going down to Widget Blueprint,

11
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.159
and then selecting our user widget as our widget base.

12
00:00:34.159 --> 00:00:37.159
So let's go ahead and we're going to pop over to the editor.

13
00:00:37.159 --> 00:00:38.079
There we go.

14
00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:40.770
And once we're inside the editor,

15
00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.130
we're going to right click on our content browser, user

16
00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.850
interface, Widget Blueprint.

17
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.810
From our pick parent class for new Widget Blueprint,

18
00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.490
we're going to select the user widget option.

19
00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:58.000
And we are going to call this HUD underscore UMG.

20
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.679
Now, once we have that done, we're

21
00:01:00.679 --> 00:01:02.640
going to double click on it to open it up.

22
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.439
And the first thing that we have to do once we open it up

23
00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:06.439
is add something called a Canvas panel.

24
00:01:06.439 --> 00:01:09.799
Now, a Canvas panel allows us to add and group

25
00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:13.560
other elements to this UMG widget.

26
00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.099
Without the Canvas panel, we'd only

27
00:01:15.099 --> 00:01:16.879
be able to put a singular button

28
00:01:16.879 --> 00:01:18.200
or a singular piece of text.

29
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.459
So the Canvas panel allows us to add multiple items

30
00:01:21.459 --> 00:01:22.519
to the same UI.

31
00:01:22.519 --> 00:01:25.030
So let's go ahead and double click on our HUD.

32
00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:26.909
And we're going to go over to the palette

33
00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:28.909
and we're going to search for CAN.

34
00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:30.150
And there's our Canvas panel.

35
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.230
So we're just going to use our left mouse button

36
00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:36.329
to drag and drop this right down onto our hierarchy.

37
00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.329
And next, what we're going to do

38
00:01:38.329 --> 00:01:42.569
is we are going to add two pieces of text, one

39
00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:45.329
for our score and one for our time.

40
00:01:45.329 --> 00:01:48.329
Then we're going to position these pieces of text

41
00:01:48.329 --> 00:01:50.769
so that they will be anchored to the left

42
00:01:50.769 --> 00:01:54.609
and the right hand corner at the very top of the screen.

43
00:01:54.609 --> 00:01:57.530
Now, to do this, let's go ahead and add the text first.

44
00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.049
So we're going to just take this text

45
00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:01.750
and again, left click, drag on the Canvas panel,

46
00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.829
left click, drag on the Canvas panel.

47
00:02:03.829 --> 00:02:05.370
Now, if I click on one of these,

48
00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.210
you're going to notice that there's this little flower.

49
00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:11.050
What this little flower icon is displaying

50
00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:15.530
is the location that that object will be pinned to

51
00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.530
or as the pivot or the initial location

52
00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.449
when the screen is enlarged or reduced in size.

53
00:02:23.449 --> 00:02:26.289
This is super helpful because this means this one UI can

54
00:02:26.289 --> 00:02:28.770
be set up so that whenever it is used

55
00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:32.009
on an ultra wide monitor or a very small phone,

56
00:02:32.009 --> 00:02:34.729
the same UI and all of the buttons and everything

57
00:02:34.729 --> 00:02:38.050
will all still go to the same location

58
00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.330
that the user expects without you actually

59
00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:44.090
having to do any extra work or create any additional assets.

60
00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:47.129
So let's go ahead and set these up.

61
00:02:47.129 --> 00:02:49.889
So we're going to select this bottom one.

62
00:02:49.889 --> 00:02:51.490
And the first thing I'm going to do

63
00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:52.770
is I'm going to hold down Control.

64
00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:54.569
I'm going to come over here to my Anchors.

65
00:02:54.569 --> 00:02:57.169
And I'm going to click right over here

66
00:02:57.169 --> 00:03:01.539
on this very right hand one that is flashing.

67
00:03:01.539 --> 00:03:04.580
And that is going to move that text block over there.

68
00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.580
And there's a couple of things I need to do.

69
00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.080
So first things first, we're going

70
00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.419
to set the text size to 64.

71
00:03:10.419 --> 00:03:12.659
Always find that it's easier to position these

72
00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:15.860
in place with the end text, the size that you want it.

73
00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.580
If you get it in position and then change the text,

74
00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.500
it's going to change how this actually looks

75
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:22.900
and give you a bad time.

76
00:03:22.939 --> 00:03:24.979
Next thing we're going to do is we're

77
00:03:24.979 --> 00:03:27.699
going to change this to size to content

78
00:03:27.699 --> 00:03:30.699
because we want this size of this

79
00:03:30.699 --> 00:03:34.860
to represent the score or the text.

80
00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.180
And we're also going to come up here to our text.

81
00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:40.689
And we're going to call this one time.

82
00:03:40.689 --> 00:03:44.180
So t and e.

83
00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:47.699
And we're going to also come down to our shape outline

84
00:03:47.699 --> 00:03:48.539
and set this.

85
00:03:48.539 --> 00:03:49.580
Whoops, not like that.

86
00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.159
We're going to set that to about a 2.

87
00:03:51.159 --> 00:03:52.300
There we go.

88
00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.099
And we also need a capital T for our time there.

89
00:03:55.099 --> 00:03:58.310
So there we go.

90
00:03:58.310 --> 00:03:59.069
There's our time.

91
00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:02.949
So now our time is obviously not in the greatest position

92
00:04:02.949 --> 00:04:06.110
because everything needs to be on the inside of this dotted

93
00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:06.590
line.

94
00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:07.629
So what we're going to do is we're

95
00:04:07.629 --> 00:04:09.009
going to go to our position here

96
00:04:09.009 --> 00:04:11.430
and set this to negative 100.

97
00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:17.589
And then we are going to set our position in the y to 100.

98
00:04:17.589 --> 00:04:19.879
And then I'm going to do something kind of cool.

99
00:04:19.879 --> 00:04:21.259
I'm going to take this alignment

100
00:04:21.259 --> 00:04:24.819
and set this to 1 by 1.

101
00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:27.339
Sorry, just 1, I mean.

102
00:04:27.339 --> 00:04:28.100
Not by 1.

103
00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:28.819
There we go.

104
00:04:28.819 --> 00:04:30.939
And what this is going to do is it's basically

105
00:04:30.939 --> 00:04:33.220
going to kind of flip our transform of this

106
00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:37.259
and put it so that it is in the inside over here.

107
00:04:37.259 --> 00:04:40.100
Without us having to go all crazy trying to position

108
00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.779
this using the x and the y, I just

109
00:04:42.779 --> 00:04:46.500
find that adjusting the alignment can help.

110
00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.939
So again, let's do this same thing over here.

111
00:04:48.939 --> 00:04:50.139
We're going to grab this.

112
00:04:50.139 --> 00:04:54.699
We're going to call this one score.

113
00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:56.819
And then, oops, unselected it.

114
00:04:56.819 --> 00:04:57.899
So we have our time.

115
00:04:57.899 --> 00:04:58.819
We have our score.

116
00:04:58.819 --> 00:05:05.500
So again, 64, size to content, line size 2.

117
00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.019
And then what we're going to do

118
00:05:07.019 --> 00:05:15.660
is we're going to go 100 and 100.

119
00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:18.009
There we go.

120
00:05:18.009 --> 00:05:19.610
And that is it.

121
00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:20.689
So we've got our score.

122
00:05:20.689 --> 00:05:21.790
We have our time.

123
00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:23.410
And the coolest part is that they're

124
00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:25.529
going to stay relative to those locations

125
00:05:25.529 --> 00:05:28.009
as our UI changes in size.

126
00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:31.129
So that's exactly the behavior that we want.

127
00:05:31.129 --> 00:05:33.170
And as you can see here, this is what we've got.

128
00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:34.050
We've got our score.

129
00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.769
We have got our time.

130
00:05:35.769 --> 00:05:37.529
Now next, what we're going to do

131
00:05:37.529 --> 00:05:41.009
is we are going to set up something called a binding.

132
00:05:41.009 --> 00:05:46.069
And a binding allows us to read from any particular value

133
00:05:46.069 --> 00:05:48.129
that we have inside of one of our blueprints

134
00:05:48.129 --> 00:05:50.769
and then relay that information in our UI.

135
00:05:50.769 --> 00:05:52.649
However, one thing to note here,

136
00:05:52.649 --> 00:05:56.050
bindings can be relatively expensive, especially

137
00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:58.910
as your game progresses and gets

138
00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:00.689
bigger and more complicated.

139
00:06:00.689 --> 00:06:05.089
For this particular project, text binding

140
00:06:05.089 --> 00:06:06.689
in this application isn't really

141
00:06:06.689 --> 00:06:09.410
going to cause that much of a performance issue.

142
00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:13.500
Again, this is something that has another way,

143
00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:16.100
but this is the most simplistic way to do this.

144
00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.779
And it could become a performance problem,

145
00:06:18.779 --> 00:06:20.459
especially if you're working on an MMO

146
00:06:20.459 --> 00:06:23.779
or some type of action RPG that

147
00:06:23.779 --> 00:06:25.420
has a very complicated interface that

148
00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.500
might be listening to a bunch of values.

149
00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:30.860
This is where you could get into problems with that.

150
00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:32.740
But for our game, we're only going

151
00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:35.699
to be having very, very few things listening to this.

152
00:06:35.699 --> 00:06:37.279
So this is all good.

153
00:06:37.279 --> 00:06:39.220
Now again, what we're going to be doing

154
00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:40.220
is creating a binding.

155
00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:42.339
And that binding is going to link text

156
00:06:42.339 --> 00:06:44.300
from our blueprint to our UI.

157
00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:47.740
And to do that, what we do is we come down to our text

158
00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.500
and we click on the menu called Bind,

159
00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:52.939
and then we select the Create Bind option.

160
00:06:52.939 --> 00:06:54.579
So let's go ahead and do that now.

161
00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:56.819
So we're going to go to our score.

162
00:06:56.819 --> 00:06:59.750
And then right here for our, actually,

163
00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:03.310
I think we need to do this, yes, for our score.

164
00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:05.029
So make sure our score is selected.

165
00:07:05.029 --> 00:07:08.060
Bind, Create Binding.

166
00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.339
And this is going to create our binding.

167
00:07:10.339 --> 00:07:12.220
But what are we actually going to be doing?

168
00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:13.759
Well, what we're going to be doing

169
00:07:13.759 --> 00:07:15.920
is creating this little bit of blueprint code.

170
00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:17.420
What this code is going to do is

171
00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:19.300
it's going to go out to our player pawn.

172
00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:21.980
It's going to cast to our vehicle blueprint,

173
00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:24.180
and then it's going to get the current score.

174
00:07:24.259 --> 00:07:26.420
And then we're going to take that current score

175
00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:28.259
and we're going to format this text

176
00:07:28.259 --> 00:07:30.339
so that it will say score,

177
00:07:30.339 --> 00:07:33.740
but the value that you see there

178
00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:36.139
will be reflected from the getCurrentScore.

179
00:07:36.139 --> 00:07:38.339
So this is really cool because this means

180
00:07:38.339 --> 00:07:40.860
that we can have a text value

181
00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:44.019
that signifies what this is and then have our number.

182
00:07:44.019 --> 00:07:46.759
And we don't actually have to manage two different widgets

183
00:07:46.759 --> 00:07:49.720
to get the same information.

184
00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:53.529
So let's go ahead and pop over to the editor now.

185
00:07:53.529 --> 00:07:54.769
And first things first,

186
00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:59.899
we are going to get player pawn.

187
00:07:59.899 --> 00:08:01.959
So there's our get player pawn.

188
00:08:01.959 --> 00:08:03.600
And then from our player pawn,

189
00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:07.620
we are going to cast to,

190
00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.459
we want our advanced vehicle pawn

191
00:08:09.459 --> 00:08:12.060
because that is the one that we're using

192
00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:13.300
for this example.

193
00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:15.160
We're going to then right click on this

194
00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:18.300
and convert to a pure cast.

195
00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.240
And once we have this in a pure cast,

196
00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:25.240
we are going to look for as the vehicle advanced pawn,

197
00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:30.709
our current, and there we go, getCurrentScore.

198
00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.330
And I'm going to pull this over here.

199
00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:33.629
So next, what we need to do

200
00:08:33.629 --> 00:08:35.149
is we're going to pull off of this

201
00:08:35.149 --> 00:08:38.049
and we're going to look for format

202
00:08:38.049 --> 00:08:43.049
and we might need to disable context sensitive.

203
00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:44.769
There we go, format text.

204
00:08:44.769 --> 00:08:47.870
So oops, just going to undo this for a second

205
00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:52.039
and go ahead and delete that.

206
00:08:52.039 --> 00:08:53.039
So there we go.

207
00:08:53.039 --> 00:08:55.320
All right, so with our format text,

208
00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.000
what we need to do first

209
00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:01.240
is we're going to put in score, semicolon,

210
00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:05.159
and then we're going to put in two curly brackets

211
00:09:05.159 --> 00:09:08.460
and then the word value.

212
00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:09.419
And when we do this,

213
00:09:09.419 --> 00:09:11.860
what we're going to get is right underneath that,

214
00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:13.139
we're going to get a value.

215
00:09:13.139 --> 00:09:15.580
So we're going to input our value

216
00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:19.929
and then we're going to take our result here

217
00:09:19.929 --> 00:09:24.370
and plug that right into our return value.

218
00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:25.730
So again, what we're going to first do

219
00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:27.389
is get our player pawn.

220
00:09:27.389 --> 00:09:29.950
We are going to cast to our vehicle advanced pawn

221
00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:33.830
because that's where we're doing all of our calculations.

222
00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:35.330
We're going to get our current score.

223
00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:36.990
And then using that value,

224
00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:41.470
we are going to first put the word score semicolon

225
00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:43.389
and then this value.

226
00:09:43.389 --> 00:09:45.690
And that is what is actually going to be added

227
00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:49.870
to our particular piece of code on the UI

228
00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:51.830
or a piece of information on the UI.

229
00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:54.700
I'm going to compile and save.

230
00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:57.639
And what we're going to do next

231
00:09:57.639 --> 00:09:59.360
is we're going to do the same thing,

232
00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:01.519
but this time with our time.

233
00:10:01.519 --> 00:10:02.919
So we're going to select our time.

234
00:10:02.919 --> 00:10:05.600
We're going to do basically get game mode,

235
00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.000
cast to our vehicle advanced game mode,

236
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.159
and then get our time remaining.

237
00:10:09.159 --> 00:10:11.769
So let's go ahead and do that now.

238
00:10:11.769 --> 00:10:14.090
So we are going to come back to our,

239
00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:16.330
not our event graph, but our designer.

240
00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:17.970
We're going to select time.

241
00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:23.740
Then remember content, text, bind, create binding.

242
00:10:23.919 --> 00:10:24.759
There we go.

243
00:10:24.759 --> 00:10:29.320
And then what we want to do is get game mode.

244
00:10:30.159 --> 00:10:34.230
So get game mode.

245
00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:35.750
There we go, get game mode.

246
00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:43.340
And then we are going to cast to,

247
00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:46.830
oh, because it's called vehicle game mode,

248
00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:47.970
vehicle advanced game mode.

249
00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:48.809
There we go.

250
00:10:48.809 --> 00:10:49.629
We're going to right click on this

251
00:10:49.629 --> 00:10:50.830
and convert it to a pure cast

252
00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.389
because we know that we are getting

253
00:10:52.389 --> 00:10:54.620
a specific value from in there.

254
00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:55.620
And what are we going to do?

255
00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:56.940
Well, we're going to pull off of this

256
00:10:56.940 --> 00:11:00.879
and we are going to get time

257
00:11:00.879 --> 00:11:07.940
and I'm going to enable context sensitivity, get time.

258
00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:08.899
There we go.

259
00:11:08.899 --> 00:11:10.879
Get time remaining.

260
00:11:10.879 --> 00:11:12.679
And what do we want to do with this?

261
00:11:12.679 --> 00:11:14.240
Well, we want to format.

